  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "State, Backends & the Environment Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Terraform state is a JSON map from config addresses to real resource IDs. No state means no knowledge of what exists."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "\"aws_instance.web\"   -> \"i-0abc123\"",
            "\"aws_db_instance.db\" -> \"db-prod-1\"",
            "# that mapping IS the state file"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Environments Hurt",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One state file = exactly one deployed instance of a config",
            "That single fact is the root of the whole problem",
            "`environment` is not a first-class Terraform concept",
            "It is only a separate state file plus separate input variables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where State Lives"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Backend",
            "State lives in",
            "Locking"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "local",
              "`terraform.tfstate`",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "s3",
              "bucket key",
              "lockfile (1.10+) or DynamoDB"
            ],
            [
              "azurerm",
              "blob",
              "blob lease"
            ],
            [
              "gcs / http",
              "object / endpoint",
              "backend-native"
            ],
            [
              "remote / HCP",
              "platform",
              "automatic"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Locking stops two concurrent applies corrupting state",
            "Backend config is block-level: no variables, no interpolation",
            "That one restriction forces the workspace-vs-directory choice"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform init -backend-config=prod.hcl",
            "# partial backend config, supplied at",
            "# init time - never at plan time"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Owns State"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Root module = the directory you run `terraform` in",
            "Child modules are called from it and own no state",
            "`terraform.tfstate.backup` written before every mutation",
            "On a remote backend the provider keeps versions instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "State Identity",
          "items": [
            "Serial number increments per write",
            "Lineage UUID identifies the state's ancestry",
            "Mismatched lineage = foreign state, Terraform refuses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Secrets Land Here"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RDS passwords and generated keys sit in state in plaintext",
            "Encrypt at rest: S3 SSE or KMS on the bucket",
            "Restrict bucket reads per environment, not per team"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform state list",
            "terraform state show aws_instance.web",
            "terraform state mv <src> <dst>",
            "terraform state rm aws_s3_bucket.old",
            "# rm forgets it, does not destroy it"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Local state",
                "lines": [
                  "fast",
                  "no locking",
                  "no sharing",
                  "no audit"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Remote state",
                "lines": [
                  "locking",
                  "sharing",
                  "audit trail",
                  "network on every cmd"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Blast radius = one state file",
          "text": "Splitting environments is really splitting blast radius. Every pattern in this handbook is a way of drawing that line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "CLI Workspaces: Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Command Surface",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform workspace new dev",
            "terraform workspace select prod",
            "terraform workspace list   # * = current",
            "terraform workspace show",
            "terraform workspace delete dev"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every config starts with one workspace named `default`",
            "`default` cannot be deleted, ever",
            "Only the state file swaps - nothing else does"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where The State Files Go"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Backend",
            "default",
            "named workspace"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "local",
              "`terraform.tfstate`",
              "`terraform.tfstate.d/<name>/`"
            ],
            [
              "s3",
              "`<key>`",
              "`env:/<name>/<key>`"
            ],
            [
              "s3 + prefix",
              "`<key>`",
              "`<prefix>/<name>/<key>`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`workspace_key_prefix` defaults to the literal string `env:`. That colon in your bucket listing is the giveaway."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Interpolation Hook"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "name = \"app-${terraform.workspace}\"",
            "locals { env = {",
            "  dev  = { size = \"t3.micro\", n = 1 }",
            "  prod = { size = \"m5.large\", n = 6 }",
            "} }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Look up settings with `local.env[terraform.workspace]`",
            "One config, one backend, one provider block, one module set",
            "Size and name vary; structure cannot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What They Do Not Isolate"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same AWS profile, same account, same region by default",
            "Credentials are shared unless you deliberately vary them",
            "`workspace delete` refuses while the state is non-empty",
            "`-force` deletes the state and orphans live infrastructure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Invisible File",
          "items": [
            "Selection lives in `.terraform/environment`",
            "Local, untracked, invisible in code review",
            "CI must run `terraform workspace select <env>`",
            "Forget it and you apply to whatever was last selected"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Fresh clone lands in default",
          "text": "`terraform init` in a new checkout puts you in `default`, not your last workspace. Nothing in the plan header warns you."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Things Named Workspace"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CLI workspaces: state keys under one backend",
            "HCP / Terraform Cloud workspaces: own variables, credentials, run history",
            "Named `environments` in 0.9, renamed in 0.10",
            "HashiCorp's own docs now warn against using them for environments"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Directory-per-Environment: Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Layout",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "repo/",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1",
                "c0_2"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0",
                "c1_1"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0",
                "c2_1",
                "c2_2"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "repo/",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "envs/"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "modules/"
              },
              "b2": {
                "text": "each env root"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "dev/"
              },
              "c0_1": {
                "text": "staging/"
              },
              "c0_2": {
                "text": "prod/"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "network/"
              },
              "c1_1": {
                "text": "app/"
              },
              "c2_0": {
                "text": "main.tf"
              },
              "c2_1": {
                "text": "backend.tf"
              },
              "c2_2": {
                "text": "terraform.tfvars"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b2"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_2"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_2"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every environment directory is its own root module",
            "Shared logic lives once in `modules/network`, `modules/app`",
            "Each root calls those modules with different inputs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Literal, Greppable Backends"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "terraform {",
            "  backend \"s3\" {",
            "    key = \"prod/app/terraform.tfstate\"",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Real Credential Isolation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "provider \"aws\" {",
            "  region = \"eu-west-1\"",
            "  assume_role {",
            "    role_arn = var.prod_role_arn",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per-environment account, `role_arn` and region",
            "Diffs are reviewable: `m5.large -> m5.xlarge` in the PR",
            "Environments may legitimately diverge - no conditional needed",
            "Prod gets a WAF and multi-AZ RDS; dev does not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What It Costs You"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cost",
            "Mitigation"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "N near-identical roots",
              "keep roots thin"
            ],
            [
              "new output = edit N files",
              "one module call + backend + tfvars"
            ],
            [
              "`init` per directory",
              "accept it; lockfiles are per-dir too"
            ],
            [
              "symlinked `.tf` files",
              "breaks on Windows, confuses `fmt`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Single-Root Hybrid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform init -backend-config=prod.hcl",
            "terraform plan -var-file=envs/prod.tfvars",
            "# one dir, per-env tfvars, but state",
            "# still has to be swapped by hand"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Pinning Per Stage",
          "items": [
            "`.terraform/` and lockfiles are per-directory",
            "Prod pins provider `5.31.0`",
            "Dev can test `5.40.0` in isolation",
            "Upgrade risk stops being all-or-nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Promotion is a diff",
          "text": "Bump the module version in dev tfvars, then staging, then prod. Explicit, auditable, and reversible by revert."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This is the layout HashiCorp, Gruntwork and most large teams recommend for real long-lived environments."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Workspaces vs Directories: Head to Head",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Isolation",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Workspaces",
            "Directories"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "State",
              "same backend, new key",
              "independent backends"
            ],
            [
              "Credentials",
              "none by default",
              "full, per provider"
            ],
            [
              "Code drift",
              "forbidden structurally",
              "permitted"
            ],
            [
              "Divergence",
              "conditionals",
              "plain separate files"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "count = terraform.workspace == \"prod\"",
            "        ? 3 : 1",
            "# multiply these and they rot"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Humans And Blast Radius"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "Workspaces",
            "Directories"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Review",
              "hidden in locals maps",
              "plain diff"
            ],
            [
              "Mistake",
              "wrong workspace, prod state",
              "you had to `cd` there"
            ],
            [
              "Onboarding",
              "tribal CLI knowledge",
              "obvious from `ls`"
            ],
            [
              "Boilerplate",
              "near zero",
              "O(N) files"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fit And Anti-Fit"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Workspaces fit",
                "lines": [
                  "per-branch previews",
                  "developer sandboxes",
                  "test fixtures",
                  "short-lived copies"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Workspaces misfit",
                "lines": [
                  "separate cloud accounts",
                  "different compliance",
                  "long-lived prod",
                  "different shapes"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hybrid that works: directories for the stage boundary",
            "Workspaces inside a stage for ephemeral feature stacks",
            "Never the reverse"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Ways Out Of O(N)"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Terragrunt sits on top of directories",
            "`terragrunt.hcl` generates the backend block and injects inputs",
            "HCP inverts it: one directory, many named cloud workspaces",
            "Each cloud workspace owns its variable set and credentials"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Which do I pick?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Differ in identity - account, credentials, compliance - use directories",
            "Differ only in size and name - workspaces are defensible",
            "Unsure? Directories. The cost is files, not incidents"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Read it as a question of identity",
          "text": "Not \"how much boilerplate do I save\" but \"are these the same system twice, or two systems that rhyme\"."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Remote Runs & Remote State",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Meanings Of Remote",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Remote state: the backend stores the state file",
            "Remote runs: plan and apply execute on a server",
            "People say `remote` and mean either one",
            "A `cloud {}` block or `backend \"remote\"` enables the second"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "cloud {",
            "  organization = \"iolar\"",
            "  workspaces { name = \"app-prod\" }",
            "}",
            "# plan now streams a remote run"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Execution Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Config runs on",
            "Credentials live"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Remote",
              "the platform",
              "on the platform"
            ],
            [
              "Local",
              "laptop or CI runner",
              "on that machine"
            ],
            [
              "Agent",
              "self-hosted runner",
              "inside your VPC"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In remote mode the config is uploaded, the run happens there, and output streams back to your terminal. Local mode stores state only."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Run Lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "plan queued",
              "policy check",
              "cost estimate",
              "awaiting confirm",
              "applied"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Policy check = Sentinel or OPA gate",
            "Speculative plan: triggered by a PR, never applyable",
            "It exists purely for review",
            "The run is bound to a named workspace, not a local file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Secrets never touch a laptop",
          "text": "Remote runs solve the credential problem workspaces cannot, and the workspace-selection footgun disappears with it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Another Stack"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "data \"terraform_remote_state\" \"net\" {",
            "  backend = \"s3\"",
            "  config = { bucket = var.b,",
            "    key = \"prod/net.tfstate\" }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Coupling Tax",
          "items": [
            "Reading state grants the whole file, secrets included",
            "Prefer published outputs, SSM parameters, or a data lookup",
            "Network must apply before app",
            "No dependency graph exists across state files"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The CI Alternative"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Atlantis: comment `atlantis plan -d envs/prod` on the PR",
            "Plan runs in a controlled runner, diff posted back",
            "Cost of remote runs: queueing latency",
            "No local `-target` debugging; egress from someone else's VPC"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Drift: What It Is and Where It Comes From",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Drift is divergence between three things that should agree: the configuration, the state file, and the real infrastructure."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Drift",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0",
                "c1_1"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0",
                "c2_1"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "Drift",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "infra drift"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "state drift"
              },
              "b2": {
                "text": "code drift"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "console change"
              },
              "c0_1": {
                "text": "real != state"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "deleted out of band"
              },
              "c1_1": {
                "text": "plan proposes create"
              },
              "c2_0": {
                "text": "prod .tf != staging .tf"
              },
              "c2_1": {
                "text": "same name, different system"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b2"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_1"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How It Is Detected",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Refresh reads every resource from the provider API before diffing",
            "`-refresh=false` skips it: faster plans, stale comparison",
            "You are then diffing against a state that may be fiction"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -refresh-only",
            "# shows drift, proposes no config change",
            "terraform apply -refresh-only",
            "# writes reality into state = accept it"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where It Comes From"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Console hotfixes during an incident",
            "Autoscaling changing `desired_count` underneath you",
            "A cloud provider defaulting a field you left blank",
            "Another Terraform config touching the same resource"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Provider-Injected Drift",
          "items": [
            "AWS adds default tags",
            "A security group grows a description",
            "The plan shows a change you never wrote",
            "Nobody touched anything - the API did"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Dangerous Shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "Symptom",
            "Why it bites"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Stage drift",
              "staging passes, prod fails",
              "prod hand-patched months ago"
            ],
            [
              "Deleted-outside",
              "plan proposes create",
              "a create in prod mid-incident"
            ],
            [
              "Silent drift",
              "plan stays empty",
              "attribute is unmanaged"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Silent drift covers an EBS volume's actual data",
            "And any tag or field Terraform does not manage",
            "It will never appear in any plan, ever"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Drift is not always a bug",
          "text": "A break-glass fix at 3am is legitimate engineering. The bug is failing to reconcile it afterwards."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why is code drift the sneaky one?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No refresh detects it - both stages are internally consistent",
            "It only surfaces when a promotion fails",
            "Comparing states, not resources, is the only way to see it"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Detecting & Reconciling Drift",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scheduled Detection",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -refresh-only \\",
            "  -detailed-exitcode",
            "# 0 = no changes",
            "# 1 = error",
            "# 2 = changes present"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Run it nightly, once per environment",
            "The exit code is the alerting hook - alert on 2",
            "HCP Terraform ships this as health assessments per workspace"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Machine-Readable Drift"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -out=tfplan",
            "terraform show -json tfplan | jq '",
            "  .resource_changes[]",
            "  | select(.change.actions != [\"no-op\"])'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Ways To Reconcile"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "Action",
            "Use when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "A revert",
              "`terraform apply`",
              "correct default"
            ],
            [
              "B adopt",
              "edit `.tf`, apply",
              "reality is right"
            ],
            [
              "C accept",
              "`apply -refresh-only`",
              "externally owned"
            ],
            [
              "D ignore",
              "`lifecycle` block",
              "another system owns it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "lifecycle {",
            "  ignore_changes = [desired_count,",
            "    tags[\"LastScanned\"]]",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Option B ends with an empty plan - that is how you know the adoption is complete, not merely applied."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Adopting The Unmanaged"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "import {",
            "  to = aws_s3_bucket.logs",
            "  id = \"my-logs\"",
            "}",
            "# 1.5+ form, visible in the plan"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform import` is the older imperative equivalent",
            "`terraform state rm` releases a resource to another config",
            "It stops managing it without destroying it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Finding Code Drift"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Diff `terraform show -json` across the dev and prod states",
            "That finds code drift, not just infra drift",
            "Nothing else will surface it before a failed promotion"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Alerts That Work",
          "items": [
            "`prod: 3 resources drifted` is actionable",
            "`drift detected` is noise",
            "Always name the environment",
            "Every console change gets a follow-up PR this sprint"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Unreconciled drift becomes permanent",
          "text": "A hotfix without a follow-up PR stops being a hotfix. It quietly becomes the design, discovered a year later."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Preventing Divergence Between Stages",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The root cause of stage drift is people, not tooling. Fix the write path, not just the detector."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Close The Write Path",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Remove human write access to prod entirely",
            "Apply only through a CI role",
            "Developers get read-only plus a break-glass procedure",
            "Immutable prod: replace infrastructure, never mutate it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Version Everything"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "module \"app\" {",
            "  source =",
            "    \"git::$ORG/inf//modules/app?ref=v1.4.2\"",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Promotion becomes a version bump, not a copy-paste",
            "Same module version everywhere: the diff is only tfvars",
            "Pin providers in `.terraform.lock.hcl` and commit it",
            "Unpinned providers drift environments apart on their own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Promote the artifact",
          "text": "The module ref that passed staging is the ref that goes to prod. Never re-run a build to produce prod's version."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Data, Not Structure"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Keep in data",
                "lines": [
                  "tfvars",
                  "settings map",
                  "sizes and counts",
                  "names and tags"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Never in structure",
                "lines": [
                  "different resource blocks",
                  "stage-only modules",
                  "forked file trees"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Gates Before Merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Catches"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`terraform fmt -check`",
              "noise diffs"
            ],
            [
              "`terraform validate`",
              "broken config"
            ],
            [
              "`tflint` / `checkov`",
              "bad patterns, insecure defaults"
            ],
            [
              "Sentinel / conftest",
              "untagged prod, public buckets"
            ],
            [
              "plan review",
              "everything else"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Make prod plans empty by default",
            "A non-empty prod plan on an unrelated PR is a signal",
            "Investigate it before merging anything"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Give Them A Sandbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bake preview environments from workspaces",
            "Cheap, disposable, per-branch",
            "Nobody hand-builds a test environment inside prod",
            "Terragrunt DRY: root `terragrunt.hcl` holds `remote_state`, children supply inputs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Make It A Metric",
          "items": [
            "Track days since last unreverted drift",
            "Per environment, on the reliability dashboard",
            "Unmeasured discipline decays quietly"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Common Mistakes & Gotchas",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Aiming At The Wrong Target",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`.terraform/environment` left on `prod` - nothing in the plan header stops you",
            "`default` holding real prod state because nobody created one",
            "`workspace delete -force` orphaning live resources",
            "One S3 key shared across environments - two applies race, state corrupts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Copying a state file",
          "text": "Best case a lineage mismatch stops you. Worst case dev silently adopts prod's resource IDs and the next destroy is real."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Configuration Rot"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Workspaces across AWS accounts: one bucket now holds every environment's secrets",
            "Fifteen `terraform.workspace` ternaries in one file, none tested for dev",
            "Secrets in tfvars committed to git",
            "State already leaks them - the repo does not need to as well"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "count    = length(var.envs)  # indexes",
            "for_each = toset(var.envs)   # keys",
            "# drop the middle item of a count list",
            "# and it destroys the wrong resource"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Process Holes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Forgetting `init` after switching directories: stale modules, or a hard error",
            "`-target` as a routine tool - skips dependents, leaves state half-applied",
            "`-refresh=false` in CI to save time, then no drift noticed for months",
            "Auto-apply on merge to main for prod with no manual gate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shortcut",
            "Bill arrives as"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-refresh=false`",
              "silent months of drift"
            ],
            [
              "routine `-target`",
              "partially applied state"
            ],
            [
              "auto-apply prod",
              "a bad plan ships at 2am"
            ],
            [
              "`-force` delete",
              "resources with no state"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "An empty plan means healthy, right?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No. Unmanaged resources never appear in a plan",
            "Neither do fields covered by `ignore_changes`",
            "Empty means \"nothing I manage changed\", not \"nothing changed\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Orphan Move"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deleting a module from code without applying first",
            "State keeps the resource; the config no longer describes it",
            "The plan can no longer manage or destroy it",
            "Order matters: apply the removal, then delete the code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cheap Guardrails",
          "items": [
            "Print the workspace in the CI log header",
            "Require a manual approval step on prod applies",
            "Fail the pipeline if `-refresh=false` appears"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Summary & Decision Playbook",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Environments in Terraform are just separate state files plus separate inputs. Every pattern here is a way to arrange those two things."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Default",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Directory-per-environment for dev, staging, prod",
            "Workspaces only for ephemeral copies",
            "Terragrunt or HCP workspaces when duplication becomes the bottleneck"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Do they differ in identity?",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "Do they differ in identity?",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "yes: accounts, compliance"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "no: only names and sizes"
              },
              "b2": {
                "text": "duplication hurts"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "directories"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "workspaces defensible"
              },
              "c2_0": {
                "text": "Terragrunt / HCP"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b2"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_0"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choose",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Workspaces",
              "same account, same shape, short-lived"
            ],
            [
              "Directories",
              "different creds or legitimate divergence"
            ],
            [
              "Terragrunt",
              "generated backends, injected inputs"
            ],
            [
              "HCP workspaces",
              "per-workspace variables and credentials"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Remote, Both Kinds"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Remote state gives locking and sharing",
            "Remote runs give credential isolation and reviewable plans",
            "Adopt both for prod",
            "Consume other stacks deliberately: outputs or SSM, not raw state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Drift In One Card"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Three flavours: infra vs state, state vs reality, code vs code",
            "Detect: scheduled `plan -refresh-only -detailed-exitcode`",
            "Alert on exit code 2, named per environment",
            "Reconcile deliberately: revert, adopt, accept, or ignore"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# nightly, per environment",
            "terraform workspace select prod",
            "terraform plan -refresh-only \\",
            "  -detailed-exitcode || alert prod"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Prevention Checklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Versioned modules, committed lockfiles",
            "No human write access to prod",
            "Policy-as-code gates before merge",
            "Differences live in tfvars, never in structure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Two health checks for any setup",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Can a new engineer tell which environment they will change, from the files alone?",
            "Is the prod plan empty right now - and do you have evidence it was empty yesterday?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The tool enforces nothing",
          "text": "Terraform will happily apply dev's config to prod's state. Repository layout and the CI pipeline are the only real discipline."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Terraform has no concept of an \"environment\" — it only has state files and input variables, and every pattern you have ever argued about is a way to arrange those two. This handbook walks CLI workspaces vs directory-per-environment vs Terragrunt, how remote runs change the credential story, and the three flavours of drift that quietly split staging from prod. Ends with a decision tree and two health checks you can run on your repo tonight.",
